1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,559
Professional and Teaching Assistant recruitment involves
applications, academic checks, reviews, and final lists.

2
00:00:06,559 --> 00:00:09,867
Manual coordination makes this process harder to manage.

3
00:00:10,367 --> 00:00:16,200
Our solution brings the complete workflow into one portal, from
generated application forms to approved results.

4
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:18,893
Administrators configure and approve.

5
00:00:18,893 --> 00:00:20,967
Students apply and track progress.

6
00:00:20,967 --> 00:00:24,167
Faculty review candidates for their assigned courses.

7
00:00:24,667 --> 00:00:30,067
The Admin dashboard shows the active semester, application counts,
filled positions, and vacancies.

8
00:00:30,567 --> 00:00:35,767
Admin sets course slots, assistantship amounts, application dates,
and course-head assignments.

9
00:00:36,267 --> 00:00:42,300
Publishing year, C G P A, grade, and interview rules generates the
opportunities and forms.

10
00:00:42,800 --> 00:00:47,400
The student starts with a preloaded academic profile, reducing
repeated data entry.

11
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:52,924
Opportunities show eligibility, available positions, requirements,
and assistantship amounts.

12
00:00:52,924 --> 00:00:55,733
The backend rechecks eligibility before submission.

13
00:00:56,233 --> 00:00:58,853
This form already contains academic details.

14
00:00:58,853 --> 00:01:01,533
The student only adds an optional statement.

15
00:01:02,033 --> 00:01:07,000
Here, two P A applications and one T A application are submitted
and tracked separately.

16
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:11,117
Faculty can access only their assigned active-semester course.

17
00:01:11,117 --> 00:01:13,100
Let us follow the review process.

18
00:01:13,600 --> 00:01:17,461
Faculty inspect the submitted academics, statement, and timetable.

19
00:01:17,461 --> 00:01:19,567
Private notes support their review.

20
00:01:20,067 --> 00:01:22,349
The candidate is shortlisted and selected.

21
00:01:22,349 --> 00:01:25,500
Capacity checks prevent the course from being overfilled.

22
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:30,867
Accepting the P A appointment automatically cancels other pending
applications for the same role.

23
00:01:31,367 --> 00:01:36,600
For the interview-required T A role, faculty schedule an interview
with its time and location.

24
00:01:37,100 --> 00:01:40,021
An evaluation must be recorded before selection.

25
00:01:40,021 --> 00:01:42,333
The T A appointment is then accepted.

26
00:01:42,833 --> 00:01:45,127
One student may hold one P A and one T A.

27
00:01:45,127 --> 00:01:47,533
Faculty submit both appointments to Admin.

28
00:01:48,033 --> 00:01:54,033
Admin reviews submitted appointments and conflicts, then finalizes
the semester, locking the approved results.

29
00:01:54,533 --> 00:01:59,500
The final selected list is generated automatically and can be
downloaded as Excel or P D F.

30
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:05,500
The student can see the other P A application automatically
cancelled, with both accepted roles retained.

31
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:10,033
Personal final results show only that student's approved
appointments and amounts.

32
00:02:10,533 --> 00:02:12,854
React and Vite provide the frontend.

33
00:02:12,854 --> 00:02:15,691
Express enforces access and workflow rules.

34
00:02:15,691 --> 00:02:20,333
PostgreSQL transactions protect appointments; local mode uses P G
Lite.

35
00:02:20,833 --> 00:02:22,685
Revocable sessions protect access.

36
00:02:22,685 --> 00:02:28,133
An optional signed intranet interface supports institutional
identity and academic synchronization.

37
00:02:28,633 --> 00:02:35,433
The expected impact is less manual entry, organized reviews,
clearer status tracking, and auditable final lists.

38
00:02:35,933 --> 00:02:38,078
This demonstration uses synthetic data.

39
00:02:38,078 --> 00:02:44,900
Real university sign-in and production hosting remain to
configure; duty timetable-overlap detection is a future extension.
